Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:26:16

Fixed. The text of the wiki chapter, the README, the window's hints, tooltips, states and messages, the full screen's
tooltips and messages, the preview's, loader's and firmware's messages and two installer messages was rewritten to the
writing standard: short sentences, one fact each, no chains, the purpose first. "Boot loader" is now written
"bootloader", and the wiki and the README explain it the first time. The question before Download now asks first and
gives one fact per line. The README links to the wiki, where it said manual. No label was renamed. The wiki said that
the open window also sends the firmware itself while Load it by itself when the camera is plugged in is off. It does
that only while the option is on, and the wiki now says so. The installer's shared messages and "Not authorized: the
password dialog was canceled or refused." keep their wording. Nothing the app does has changed. In
tests/test_main_window.py the test of the screenshot without a picture now looks for the new wording.

